# Workflow

- Skills: use `/plan-issue <N>` to plan and `/implement-issue <N>` to execute (`.cursor/skills/`). Plan first for anything non-trivial (all `science` issues, anything touching the trace schema or cost table).
- **Picking work:** lowest-numbered open issue whose `> Blocked by #N` blockers are all merged (issue number = build order). #22 must be merged before any other M6 issue.
- One issue per branch/PR. Branch: `issue-<n>-<slug>`. Never commit to `main` directly. PR title: `[M#] #<issue>: <title>`. Body: `Closes #N` + how each acceptance-criteria checkbox is met + deviations + test/perf evidence.
- Every AC checkbox needs a test where testable. Never quietly drop scope — flag impossibilities in the PR description.
- Keep PRs under ~600 changed lines (excluding lockfiles/fixtures) — split otherwise. Incidental refactors go in separate PRs.
- CI (typecheck + vitest + lint) must be green locally before opening the PR. **Claude reviews every PR before merge; never self-merge** (see `no-self-merge.mdc`).
- Discovered work (bugs, follow-ups, ambiguities) becomes a new GitHub issue — never scope creep in the current PR.
- **CI red on `main` is stop-the-line:** file a bug issue and fix it before any task work.
- New runtime dependencies require written justification in the PR (static-page bundle budget).
